# LLM usage in this A2A agent

## Configuration and secrets

- **Never** hardcode API keys or tokens. Read from environment (e.g. `os.environ`, `pydantic-settings`) and document required variables in **README.md** (names only; no real values). Add keys to `.env` locally; keep `.env` out of git.
- Centralize **model id**, **temperature**, **max tokens**, and **base URL** (if applicable) in one place (module-level constants, a small `settings` object, or env-backed config)—avoid scattering magic strings across `Agent.run`.

## Dependencies

- Declare the official client/SDK in **`pyproject.toml`**, then run **`uv lock`** / **`uv sync`** and commit **`uv.lock`**. Prefer maintained, async-capable clients when `Agent.run` stays async.

## Integration with A2A (`Agent.run`)

- Use **`TaskUpdater`**: call `update_status` / `add_artifact` so long-running LLM work surfaces progress (e.g. “Calling model…”) instead of blocking silently.
- On failure, raise or propagate errors the **`Executor`** can turn into a failed task; avoid returning raw stack traces or provider error bodies as the only user-visible text—summarize safely, log details server-side if needed.

## Robustness and safety

- Set **timeouts** and **retries** where the SDK allows; handle rate limits and empty responses explicitly.
- Treat model output as **untrusted** when used in tools, subprocesses, or downstream HTTP; validate or allowlist actions.
- **Prompts**: keep system/developer prompts in versioned code or clearly named constants; when behavior depends on prompt wording, note that in docstrings or README.

## Testing

- **Unit tests** must not call live models by default: mock the client or inject a fake implementation so CI stays deterministic and free of secrets.
